{% comment %}
╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
║  PHOTO ROLODEX — LavaEndpoint: game                             ║
║                                                                  ║
║  Paste this whole file into the CodeTemplate field of a         ║
║  LavaEndpoint named "game" (HTTP Method: GET) that belongs to    ║
║  the "rolodex" LavaApplication.                                  ║
║                                                                  ║
║  Requires Rock RMS 18.0 or later. This project targets 18.0+     ║
║  exclusively -- see DEPLOYMENT.md for why.                        ║
║                                                                  ║
║  Endpoint settings (Admin Tools > CMS > Lava Applications):      ║
║    Slug:                 game                                    ║
║    HTTP Method:          Get                                      ║
║    Enabled Lava Commands: sql                                     ║
║    Security Mode:        Application (inherit the app's grants)  ║
║    Caching:              Never (every render depends on live     ║
║                           query-string state)                    ║
║                                                                  ║
║  This template returns ONLY the inner content that goes inside  ║
║  the host page's <div id="rolodex-app">...</div> -- it must     ║
║  NOT re-emit that wrapping div itself.                           ║
║                                                                  ║
║  SOURCES ARE PERSON TAGS. Earlier drafts of this project used     ║
║  Groups and Data Views as selectable sources, with a hardcoded    ║
║  CONFIGURATION block that had to be hand-edited and kept in sync  ║
║  across two files. That's gone -- the deck is now built from      ║
║  whoever is tagged with the Tag the player picked on the setup    ║
║  screen (see rolodex-endpoint-setup.lava), which is Rock's own    ║
║  native "make a list of people" feature. Adding a new list is     ║
║  now just tagging people in Rock -- no Lava editing required.     ║
║                                                                  ║
║  Verified against a real, working reference build in this repo  ║
║  (the Cascade Hills Student Lookup Lava Application) rather than ║
║  assumed:                                                        ║
║    - QueryString.key reads a query-string value (dot notation,   ║
║      not QueryString['key']).                                    ║
║    - AsInteger is the real filter for string-to-int conversion.  ║
║      There is no "ToInteger" filter in Rock's Lava -- earlier     ║
║      drafts of this project used it and would have failed on     ║
║      every single numeric conversion in the whole game.          ║
║    - AsInteger returns null (not 0) when the input is blank or   ║
║      non-numeric, so every conversion below explicitly guards    ║
║      for that instead of assuming a zero fallback.               ║
║    - Calling another endpoint from hx-get/hx-post uses the        ║
║      "^/{applicationSlug}/{endpointSlug}" shorthand, not a        ║
║      hand-built /api/v2/lava-app/... path.                       ║
║    - {% sql %} takes named parameters (paramName:'{{ value }}'   ║
║      then @paramName in the query body) for scalar values,        ║
║      rather than interpolating {{ value }} directly into the SQL  ║
║      text. This is Rock's own documented safe pattern for SQL     ║
║      Lava. The one exception is the two IN (...) clauses below,   ║
║      which take a variable-length list of ids -- standard SQL     ║
║      parameters can't bind a list, so those still go through the  ║
║      AsInteger-forced sanitization built for that specific case.  ║
║    - TaggedItem links to a tagged Person through EntityGuid, not  ║
║      an EntityId column (confirmed against                        ║
║      Rock.Model.TaggedItem) -- the join below is on p.Guid, not   ║
║      p.Id.                                                        ║
║                                                                  ║
║  NOTE ON BROWSER URL: unlike the original HTML-block version,    ║
║  a LavaEndpoint's own URL is a bare API path with no Rock page   ║
║  chrome. Pushing that raw URL into the address bar would make a  ║
║  browser refresh show an unstyled fragment with no header/nav.   ║
║  So this version does NOT use hx-push-url -- refreshing the      ║
║  browser always returns to the setup screen on the host page.    ║
║  If you want mid-game refresh/shareable URLs preserved, that      ║
║  needs an extra layer (the host page reading its own query        ║
║  string and this endpoint setting an HX-Push-Url response header  ║
║  back to the host page's URL) -- ask if you want that built.      ║
║                                                                  ║
║  OPTIONAL "MORE ABOUT THIS PERSON" PANEL: the "minfo" query        ║
║  param (checkbox on the setup screen, default on) controls a      ║
║  collapsed <details> panel shown after you answer/reveal a card,  ║
║  surfacing campus, connection status, how long they've been       ║
║  tagged, household members, and up to 3 other non-family groups   ║
║  they belong to. It's opt-in and collapsed-by-default on purpose ║
║  -- the core loop stays a fast recall drill; the extra context    ║
║  is a tap away, not forced.                                       ║
╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %}
  ^/{applicationSlug}/{endpointSlug} is Rock's shorthand for calling a Lava
  Endpoint from hx-get/hx-post -- update "rolodex" if you use a different
  LavaApplication slug or rename either endpoint's slug.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign gameUrl  = '^/rolodex/game' %}
{% assign setupUrl = '^/rolodex/setup' %}

{% comment %}── Read the incoming request's query string ────────────────────────
  Lava Endpoints expose the request via the QueryString merge field
  (dot notation, e.g. QueryString.tag), not the PageParameter filter
  blocks use. Every value defaults to an empty string when the key is
  absent so the rest of the template can compare against '' uniformly.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign p_tag = '' %}
{% if QueryString.tag %}{% assign p_tag = QueryString.tag %}{% endif %}
{% assign p_mode = '' %}
{% if QueryString.mode %}{% assign p_mode = QueryString.mode %}{% endif %}
{% assign p_trk = '' %}
{% if QueryString.trk %}{% assign p_trk = QueryString.trk %}{% endif %}
{% assign p_deck = '' %}
{% if QueryString.deck %}{% assign p_deck = QueryString.deck %}{% endif %}
{% assign p_idx = '' %}
{% if QueryString.idx %}{% assign p_idx = QueryString.idx %}{% endif %}
{% assign p_sc = '' %}
{% if QueryString.sc %}{% assign p_sc = QueryString.sc %}{% endif %}
{% assign p_choice = '' %}
{% if QueryString.choice %}{% assign p_choice = QueryString.choice %}{% endif %}
{% assign p_choices = '' %}
{% if QueryString.choices %}{% assign p_choices = QueryString.choices %}{% endif %}
{% assign p_minfo = '' %}
{% if QueryString.minfo %}{% assign p_minfo = QueryString.minfo %}{% endif %}

{% comment %}── Apply defaults ──────────────────────────────────────────────────{% endcomment %}
{% if p_mode == '' %}{% assign p_mode = 'flip' %}{% endif %}

{% comment %}
  AsInteger returns null (not 0) for a blank or non-numeric string, so
  every conversion here is guarded explicitly rather than trusting a
  zero fallback from the filter itself.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign idx = 0 %}
{% if p_idx != '' %}{% assign idx = p_idx | AsInteger %}{% endif %}
{% assign sc = 0 %}
{% if p_sc != '' %}{% assign sc = p_sc | AsInteger %}{% endif %}
{% assign choiceId = 0 %}
{% if p_choice != '' %}{% assign choiceId = p_choice | AsInteger %}{% endif %}
{% assign trackScore = false %}
{% if p_trk == '1' %}{% assign trackScore = true %}{% endif %}
{% assign showMoreInfo = false %}
{% if p_minfo == '1' %}{% assign showMoreInfo = true %}{% endif %}

{% comment %}── Parse the tag id ─────────────────────────────────────────────────{% endcomment %}
{% assign tagId = 0 %}
{% if p_tag != '' %}{% assign tagId = p_tag | AsInteger %}{% endif %}

{% comment %}── Build shuffled deck on first game request (no deck param yet) ────{% endcomment %}
{% if p_deck == '' and p_tag != '' %}
  {% comment %}
    SQL Server doesn't allow ORDER BY NEWID() combined directly with
    SELECT DISTINCT -- ORDER BY items must appear in the select list
    whenever DISTINCT is used, and NEWID() isn't selected. The DISTINCT
    dedup happens in the inner query (in case someone was tagged more
    than once with the same tag); the outer query has no DISTINCT of its
    own, so ordering it by NEWID() is unrestricted.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% sql tagId:'{{ tagId }}' %}
    SELECT Id
    FROM (
      SELECT DISTINCT p.Id
      FROM TaggedItem ti
      JOIN Person p ON p.Guid = ti.EntityGuid
      WHERE ti.TagId              = @tagId
        AND p.PhotoId              IS NOT NULL
        AND p.RecordStatusValueId  = 3
    ) AS TaggedPeople
    ORDER BY NEWID()
  {% endsql %}
  {% assign p_deck = '' %}
  {% for row in results %}
    {% if p_deck == '' %}
      {% assign p_deck = row.Id %}
    {% else %}
      {% assign p_deck = p_deck | Append:',' | Append:row.Id %}
    {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
{% endif %}

{% comment %}── Deck state ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────{% endcomment %}
{% comment %}
  Guard: '' | Split:',' returns [''] in .NET (size 1), not [] (size 0).
  Explicitly zero out totalCards when the deck string is empty.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign deckIds    = p_deck | Split:',' %}
{% assign totalCards = deckIds | Size %}
{% if p_deck == '' %}{% assign totalCards = 0 %}{% endif %}

{% comment %}
  Security: p_deck and p_choices come straight off the query string,
  and the distractor/restore queries below interpolate them into a
  SQL IN(). A variable-length list can't be bound as a single named
  SQL parameter, so this is the one place values still get built into
  a string before hitting SQL -- AsInteger forces every element to a
  real integer (or 0 if it isn't one) first, so nothing but digits and
  commas can ever reach the query text.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign safeDeckCsv = '' %}
{% for d in deckIds %}
  {% assign dInt = 0 %}
  {% if d != '' %}{% assign dInt = d | AsInteger %}{% endif %}
  {% if dInt == null %}{% assign dInt = 0 %}{% endif %}
  {% if forloop.first %}
    {% assign safeDeckCsv = dInt %}
  {% else %}
    {% assign safeDeckCsv = safeDeckCsv | Append:',' | Append:dInt %}
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% comment %}── Fetch current card ──────────────────────────────────────────────{% endcomment %}
{% assign currentId  = 0 %}
{% assign personName = '' %}
{% assign photoId    = 0 %}

{% if totalCards > 0 and idx < totalCards %}
  {% assign currentId = 0 %}
  {% if deckIds[idx] != '' %}{% assign currentId = deckIds[idx] | AsInteger %}{% endif %}

  {% comment %}
    CampusName, ConnectionStatus, and TaggedSince are cheap scalar
    left-joins added here regardless of showMoreInfo -- they're cheap on
    a query that already runs every card, so it's simpler to always
    select them and only decide whether to *display* them down in the
    HTML. TaggedSince comes from TaggedItem.CreatedDateTime for this
    specific tag + person combination (a real Model<T> audit column, so
    it's always populated the moment someone is tagged).
  {% endcomment %}
  {% sql currentId:'{{ currentId }}' tagId:'{{ tagId }}' %}
    SELECT
      p.Id,
      COALESCE(NULLIF(p.NickName,''), p.FirstName) AS DisplayFirst,
      p.LastName,
      p.PhotoId,
      p.PrimaryFamilyId,
      cs.Value AS ConnectionStatus,
      c.Name AS CampusName,
      ti.CreatedDateTime AS TaggedSince
    FROM Person p
    LEFT JOIN DefinedValue cs ON cs.Id = p.ConnectionStatusValueId
    LEFT JOIN Campus c ON c.Id = p.PrimaryCampusId
    LEFT JOIN TaggedItem ti ON ti.TagId = @tagId AND ti.EntityGuid = p.Guid
    WHERE p.Id = @currentId
  {% endsql %}
  {% assign curPerson  = results | First %}
  {% assign personName = curPerson.DisplayFirst | Append:' ' | Append:curPerson.LastName %}
  {% assign photoId    = curPerson.PhotoId %}

  {% comment %}── More-info lookups: household + other groups (only when enabled) ─
    Two extra queries per card, only run when the player has the "Show
    more about each person" checkbox on -- no reason to pay for these
    joins when the feature is off.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% comment %}
    Initialize as real empty arrays via FromJSON rather than '' | Split:','
    -- that pattern (used deliberately elsewhere in this file for the CSV
    deck/choices strings) actually returns a 1-element array containing an
    empty string, not a 0-length array, which would make the .size > 0
    checks below always true. '[]' | FromJSON gives a genuine empty list.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% assign familyMembers = '[]' | FromJSON %}
  {% assign otherGroups   = '[]' | FromJSON %}
  {% if showMoreInfo %}
    {% if curPerson.PrimaryFamilyId %}
      {% sql currentId:'{{ currentId }}' familyId:'{{ curPerson.PrimaryFamilyId }}' %}
        SELECT
          fm.Id,
          COALESCE(NULLIF(fm.NickName,''), fm.FirstName) AS DisplayFirst,
          fm.LastName
        FROM GroupMember gm
        JOIN Person fm ON fm.Id = gm.PersonId
        WHERE gm.GroupId = @familyId AND fm.Id != @currentId
        ORDER BY fm.BirthYear
      {% endsql %}
      {% assign familyMembers = results %}
    {% endif %}

    {% comment %}
      Excludes the Family group type -- people you live with are already
      shown above as "Household." There's no "group being played" to
      exclude anymore since sources are Tags, not Groups. [Group] is
      bracket-wrapped because it's a reserved SQL Server keyword.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% sql currentId:'{{ currentId }}' %}
      SELECT TOP 3 g.Name
      FROM GroupMember gm
      JOIN [Group] g ON g.Id = gm.GroupId
      JOIN GroupType gt ON gt.Id = g.GroupTypeId
      WHERE gm.PersonId           = @currentId
        AND gm.GroupMemberStatus  = 1
        AND g.IsActive            = 1
        AND g.IsArchived          = 0
        AND g.IsSecurityRole      = 0
        AND gt.Guid              != '790E3215-3B10-442B-AF69-616C0DCB998E'
      ORDER BY gm.DateTimeAdded DESC
    {% endsql %}
    {% assign otherGroups = results %}
  {% endif %}

  {% comment %}
    Pre-build the whole info panel once here (rather than in the flip/quiz
    markup below) so the same markup can be reused in both modes without
    duplicating it -- Lava has no macro/function construct, so a captured
    variable is the standard way to share a block of rendered HTML.
    moreInfoHtml stays an empty string when showMoreInfo is off, so both
    call sites below can print it unconditionally.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% assign moreInfoHtml = '' %}
  {% if showMoreInfo %}
    {% capture moreInfoHtml %}
      <details class="rd-more-info mt-2">
        <summary class="btn btn-default btn-block">More about {{ personName }}</summary>
        <div class="rd-more-info-body mt-2">
          {% if curPerson.CampusName %}<p class="mb-1"><strong>Campus:</strong> {{ curPerson.CampusName }}</p>{% endif %}
          {% if curPerson.ConnectionStatus %}<p class="mb-1"><strong>Connection Status:</strong> {{ curPerson.ConnectionStatus }}</p>{% endif %}
          {% if curPerson.TaggedSince %}<p class="mb-1"><strong>Tagged since:</strong> {{ curPerson.TaggedSince | Date:'MMMM yyyy' }}</p>{% endif %}
          {% if familyMembers.size > 0 %}
            <p class="mb-1"><strong>Household:</strong>
              {% for fm in familyMembers %}{{ fm.DisplayFirst }} {{ fm.LastName }}{% unless forloop.last %}, {% endunless %}{% endfor %}
            </p>
          {% endif %}
          {% if otherGroups.size > 0 %}
            <p class="mb-0"><strong>Also part of:</strong>
              {% for og in otherGroups %}{{ og.Name }}{% unless forloop.last %}, {% endunless %}{% endfor %}
            </p>
          {% endif %}
          {% if curPerson.CampusName == null and curPerson.ConnectionStatus == null and curPerson.TaggedSince == null and familyMembers.size == 0 and otherGroups.size == 0 %}
            <p class="text-muted mb-0">No additional information on file.</p>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      </details>
    {% endcapture %}
  {% endif %}

  {% comment %}── Quiz choices ──────────────────────────────────────────────────{% endcomment %}
  {% if p_mode == 'quiz' %}
    {% if p_choices == '' %}
      {% comment %} First visit to this card: generate randomized choices via CTE {% endcomment %}
      {% sql currentId:'{{ currentId }}' %}
        WITH distractors AS (
          SELECT TOP 3
            p.Id,
            COALESCE(NULLIF(p.NickName,''), p.FirstName) AS DisplayFirst,
            p.LastName
          FROM Person p
          WHERE p.Id IN ({{ safeDeckCsv }}) AND p.Id != @currentId
          ORDER BY NEWID()
        ),
        correct AS (
          SELECT
            p.Id,
            COALESCE(NULLIF(p.NickName,''), p.FirstName) AS DisplayFirst,
            p.LastName
          FROM Person p
          WHERE p.Id = @currentId
        ),
        all_choices AS (
          SELECT Id, DisplayFirst, LastName FROM correct
          UNION ALL
          SELECT Id, DisplayFirst, LastName FROM distractors
        )
        SELECT Id, DisplayFirst, LastName FROM all_choices ORDER BY NEWID()
      {% endsql %}
      {% assign quizChoices = results %}
      {% comment %} Build choices param string so answer request can restore order {% endcomment %}
      {% assign p_choices = '' %}
      {% for c in quizChoices %}
        {% if p_choices == '' %}
          {% assign p_choices = c.Id %}
        {% else %}
          {% assign p_choices = p_choices | Append:',' | Append:c.Id %}
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    {% else %}
      {% comment %} Answer state: restore choices in original display order {% endcomment %}
      {% assign choiceIdList = p_choices | Split:',' %}
      {% comment %} Security: sanitize p_choices the same way as p_deck before it hits SQL. {% endcomment %}
      {% assign safeChoicesCsv = '' %}
      {% for cid in choiceIdList %}
        {% assign cidInt = 0 %}
        {% if cid != '' %}{% assign cidInt = cid | AsInteger %}{% endif %}
        {% if cidInt == null %}{% assign cidInt = 0 %}{% endif %}
        {% if forloop.first %}
          {% assign safeChoicesCsv = cidInt %}
        {% else %}
          {% assign safeChoicesCsv = safeChoicesCsv | Append:',' | Append:cidInt %}
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
      {% sql %}
        SELECT p.Id, COALESCE(NULLIF(p.NickName,''), p.FirstName) AS DisplayFirst, p.LastName
        FROM Person p
        WHERE p.Id IN ({{ safeChoicesCsv }})
      {% endsql %}
      {% assign choicePool = results %}
    {% endif %}
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% comment %}── URL building helpers ────────────────────────────────────────────{% endcomment %}
{% comment %}
  Security: p_tag and p_mode are strings lifted straight from the
  query string and get echoed back into href / hx-get attributes on
  every screen. UrlEncode them before rebuilding any URL so a crafted
  query string can't break out of the attribute and inject markup.
  deck is rebuilt from safeDeckCsv (integers only) rather than the
  raw p_deck string for the same reason.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign safeTag  = p_tag  | UrlEncode %}
{% assign safeMode = p_mode | UrlEncode %}
{% assign trkVal = '0' %}{% if trackScore %}{% assign trkVal = '1' %}{% endif %}
{% assign minfoVal = '0' %}{% if showMoreInfo %}{% assign minfoVal = '1' %}{% endif %}
{% assign baseGame    = gameUrl | Append:'?tag=' | Append:safeTag | Append:'&mode=' | Append:safeMode | Append:'&trk=' | Append:trkVal | Append:'&minfo=' | Append:minfoVal | Append:'&deck=' | Append:safeDeckCsv %}
{% assign nextIdx     = idx | Plus:1 %}
{% assign newSc       = sc %}
{% if p_choice != '' and choiceId == currentId %}{% assign newSc = sc | Plus:1 %}{% endif %}
{% assign nextCardUrl = baseGame | Append:'&idx=' | Append:nextIdx | Append:'&sc=' | Append:newSc %}
{% assign playAgainUrl = gameUrl | Append:'?tag=' | Append:safeTag | Append:'&mode=' | Append:safeMode | Append:'&trk=' | Append:trkVal | Append:'&minfo=' | Append:minfoVal %}

{% comment %}━━━━ HTML ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━{% endcomment %}

{% comment %}── Empty source ──{% endcomment %}
{% if totalCards == 0 %}

  <div class="alert alert-warning">
    {% if p_tag == '' %}
      <strong>No list selected.</strong>
      Go back and choose one to start.
    {% else %}
      <strong>No people found.</strong>
      Nobody tagged with this list has a profile photo yet.
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  <a href="#" hx-get="{{ setupUrl }}" hx-target="#rolodex-app" class="btn btn-default btn-lg btn-block">
    <i class="fa fa-arrow-left"></i>&nbsp; Back
  </a>

{% comment %}── All cards done ──{% endcomment %}
{% elsif idx >= totalCards %}

  <div class="text-center py-4">
    <i class="fa fa-trophy text-warning" style="font-size: 3rem;"></i>
    <h2 class="mt-3">All done!</h2>
    <p class="text-muted">
      You reviewed all <strong>{{ totalCards }}</strong> people.
    </p>
    {% if p_mode == 'quiz' and trackScore %}
      {% assign pct = newSc | Times:100 | DividedBy:totalCards, 0 %}
      <div class="mb-4" style="font-size: 1.25rem;">
        <strong>{{ newSc }} / {{ totalCards }}</strong> correct ({{ pct }}%)
      </div>
    {% endif %}
    <a href="#" hx-get="{{ playAgainUrl }}" hx-target="#rolodex-app" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg btn-block mb-2">
      <i class="fa fa-refresh"></i>&nbsp; Play Again
    </a>
    <a href="#" hx-get="{{ setupUrl }}" hx-target="#rolodex-app" class="btn btn-default btn-lg btn-block">
      Change List
    </a>
  </div>

{% comment %}── Active card ──{% endcomment %}
{% else %}

  {% comment %}── Header: back / progress counter / score ──{% endcomment %}
  <div class="d-flex align-items-center justify-content-between mb-2">
    <a href="#" hx-get="{{ setupUrl }}" hx-target="#rolodex-app" class="btn btn-default btn-sm">
      <i class="fa fa-arrow-left"></i>
    </a>
    <span class="text-muted small">{{ idx | Plus:1 }} / {{ totalCards }}</span>
    {% if p_mode == 'quiz' and trackScore %}
      {% comment %}
        Use newSc, not sc: newSc already reflects this card's
        just-submitted answer (see "URL building helpers" above).
        Displaying sc here would leave the score looking stale by
        one card on the post-answer view.
      {% endcomment %}
      <span class="text-muted small">{{ newSc }} correct</span>
    {% else %}
      <span></span>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  {% comment %}── Progress bar: Rock's native progress component ──{% endcomment %}
  {% assign pct = idx | Times:100 | DividedBy:totalCards, 0 %}
  <div class="progress mb-3">
    <div class="progress-bar" role="progressbar" style="width: {{ pct }}%;"
         aria-valuenow="{{ pct }}" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100"></div>
  </div>

  {% comment %}── Photo ──{% endcomment %}
  <div class="rd-photo-card rounded-lg shadow-md bg-gray-100 overflow-hidden mb-3">
    <img src="/GetImage.ashx?Id={{ photoId }}&maxWidth=600" alt="Guess who?"
         class="w-100 h-100 object-cover" style="object-position: center top;" />
  </div>

  {% comment %}────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      FLIP MODE — pure CSS details/summary reveal.
      Clicking the summary opens the details element;
      CSS hides the summary once open and reveals the name + Next link.
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────{% endcomment %}
  {% if p_mode == 'flip' %}
    <details class="rd-flip-details">
      <summary class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Tap to Reveal Name</summary>
      <h2 class="text-center my-3">{{ personName }}</h2>
      {{ moreInfoHtml }}
      <a href="#" hx-get="{{ nextCardUrl }}" hx-target="#rolodex-app" class="btn btn-success btn-lg btn-block mt-2">
        Next &nbsp;<i class="fa fa-arrow-right"></i>
      </a>
    </details>
  {% endif %}

  {% comment %}────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      QUIZ MODE
      Pre-answer:  4 choice buttons, each is an HTMX link.
      Post-answer: disabled colored buttons + result text + Next link.
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────{% endcomment %}
  {% if p_mode == 'quiz' %}

    {% if p_choice == '' %}

      {% comment %}── Pre-answer: choice buttons ──{% endcomment %}
      <div class="rd-choices-grid d-grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 mb-3">
        {% for c in quizChoices %}
          {% assign choiceUrl = baseGame | Append:'&idx=' | Append:idx | Append:'&sc=' | Append:sc | Append:'&choices=' | Append:p_choices | Append:'&choice=' | Append:c.Id %}
          <a href="#" hx-get="{{ choiceUrl }}" hx-target="#rolodex-app" class="btn btn-default btn-lg">
            {{ c.DisplayFirst }} {{ c.LastName }}
          </a>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>

    {% else %}

      {% comment %}── Post-answer: colored buttons restored in original order ──{% endcomment %}
      <div class="rd-choices-grid d-grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 mb-3">
        {% for cid in choiceIdList %}
          {% comment %}
            Compare as integers on both sides, not raw strings. cid
            comes from splitting the choices query param and row.Id
            comes back from SQL -- AsInteger both first so formatting
            differences can't cause a false negative.
          {% endcomment %}
          {% assign cidInt = 0 %}
          {% if cid != '' %}{% assign cidInt = cid | AsInteger %}{% endif %}
          {% if cidInt == null %}{% assign cidInt = 0 %}{% endif %}
          {% for row in choicePool %}
            {% assign rowIdInt = row.Id | AsInteger %}
            {% if rowIdInt == cidInt %}
              {% if cidInt == currentId %}
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-success btn-lg" disabled>
                  {{ row.DisplayFirst }} {{ row.LastName }}&nbsp;<i class="fa fa-check"></i>
                </button>
              {% elsif cidInt == choiceId %}
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-danger btn-lg" disabled>
                  {{ row.DisplayFirst }} {{ row.LastName }}
                </button>
              {% else %}
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-default btn-lg o-50" disabled>
                  {{ row.DisplayFirst }} {{ row.LastName }}
                </button>
              {% endif %}
            {% endif %}
          {% endfor %}
        {% endfor %}
      </div>

      <div style="font-size: 1.1rem;">
        {% if choiceId == currentId %}
          <span class="text-success"><i class="fa fa-check"></i>&nbsp; Correct!</span>
        {% else %}
          <span class="text-danger"><i class="fa fa-times"></i>&nbsp; That's {{ personName }}</span>
        {% endif %}
      </div>

      {{ moreInfoHtml }}

      <div class="text-center mt-3">
        <a href="#" hx-get="{{ nextCardUrl }}" hx-target="#rolodex-app" class="btn btn-default btn-lg">
          Next &nbsp;<i class="fa fa-arrow-right"></i>
        </a>
      </div>

    {% endif %}

  {% endif %}

{% endif %}
